WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.112
Here we make the behavior of WHERE very clear We
create three

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.914
sample rows one with TRUE one with FALSE and one
with UNKNOWN

00:00:10.346 --> 00:00:15.479
Then we use the Boolean field directly in the WHERE
clause Before

00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:20.223
running the example predict what will happen Only
the TRUE row will

00:00:20.236 --> 00:00:26.481
remain FALSE is removed and UNKNOWN is also removed
Click

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:31.146
Run in the browser to confirm this You can copy the
same

00:00:31.172 --> 00:00:36.251
SQL into pgAdmin if you want to experiment For
example you could

00:00:36.277 --> 00:00:40.877
change the values or add another row This small
example is important

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.550
because later when null appears in a comparison the
result may become

00:00:44.576 --> 00:00:47.952
UNKNOWN and disappear from your query even though
you did not explicitly

00:00:47.978 --> 00:00:49.331
ask SQL to remove it
